SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agios Georgios\, Pyli (horse races)
LOCATION:Pyli\, Kos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Pyli celebrates Agios Georgios with the island's traditional horse races: after the liturgy\, riders from the village race bareback on the plain below Pyli\, then there is a glendi with food and music on the square. If 23 April falls in Lent it moves to Easter Monday. Asfendiou has its own Agios Georgios the same day\, with mezedes in the little forest.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kos/#pyli-panigiri-of-agios-georgios-pyli-horse-races
